    what: 'A probability is a long-run frequency: “58% home win” means that, across many games with the same pregame profile, the home team wins about 58 of 100. Confidence on the site means two things: how far from 50% the probability sits, and how much the six models agree.', why: 'A forecast is not a pick. Reading 58% as “the home team will win” is the most common mistake in sports prediction.',
